{{--
  The account-state banner (plan §7.5, §13.5).

  Rendered by the app layout on every screen, above the topbar, when the
  workspace's billing needs attention. Two states and no more, because a
  banner that appears for everything is a banner nobody reads:

    past_due  — a charge failed. Nothing has been taken away; the point of the
                banner is that the customer finds out before the period ends.
    at a cap  — the plan is full. Only shown to the owner, who is the only
                person who can do anything about it.
--}}
{{--
  `lists` is a quota the demo domain contributes, so it is read through a
  guard rather than dereferenced: a build with that module removed has no
  such key (see docs/modules.md), and an unguarded `usage.lists.isFull`
  would throw on every screen in the app rather than on one.

  Plain `&&` rather than `?.` on purpose — Edge's expression parser is a
  subset of JavaScript and no template here relies on optional chaining.
--}}
@let(listsFull = usage && usage.lists && usage.lists.isFull)
@let(seatsFull = usage && usage.seats && usage.seats.isFull)

@if(organization.status === 'past_due')
  <div class="account-banner account-banner-danger" role="status">
    <span>
      <strong>We could not take payment.</strong>
      Nothing has been taken away — your team, lists and todos are exactly where they were.
      Update your card to keep the plan.
    </span>
    @if(isOwner && hasRoute('billing.index'))
      <a href="{{ urlFor('billing.index') }}">Update payment method</a>
    @end
  </div>
@elseif(isOwner && (listsFull || seatsFull) && hasRoute('billing.index'))
  <div class="account-banner" role="status">
    <span>
      <strong>
        {{ listsFull && seatsFull
          ? 'You are out of lists and seats.'
          : listsFull
            ? `You are using all ${usage.lists.limit} of your lists.`
            : `You are using all ${usage.seats.limit} of your seats.` }}
      </strong>
      Everything you have keeps working — only creating something new is blocked.
    </span>
    <a href="{{ urlFor('billing.index') }}">See plans</a>
  </div>
@end
